    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** centers on **Corbin Carroll**, who commands the day's highest efficiency score at 76.69. He is a priority start against Pallante, benefiting from an advantageous platoon split and a slow delivery profile from the mound that keeps his stolen base equity high. **Brice Turang** (70.18) and **Jose Caballero** (69.99) round out the top tier of our active roster. **Jose Caballero** represents a massive value play today; despite batting eighth, his dynamic platoon edge against Valdez, F (L) and the high probability of a successful bag swipe against a slow-moving pitcher elevate his output well beyond his base projection.\n\nOur most difficult decision revolved around the final utility spot, where **Kyle Karros** (57.99) narrowly edged out the remaining bench depth. **Kyle Karros** benefits significantly from a +14% park factor, which allowed him to outperform several higher-base hitters whose matchups were neutralized by stricter platoon disadvantages or tougher opposing arms. We are monitoring **James Wood** closely; while his 51.16 score is respectable, his matchup against a high-efficiency catcher (1.88s pop time) and a competent Mayza (L) creates a slight cap on his stolen base upside. We remain sidelined on **Josh Naylor**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Seiya Suzuki** due to either schedule gaps or the unfortunate rainout of the latter, ensuring we preserve our daily game caps for more favorable conditions. No additional roster moves are pending for **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Carson Williams**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, or **Henry Bolte** at this time.",
